   "target": "aptos_experimental::extracted_bulk_order_utils::cancel_at_price_level",
   "task_id": "TR-cancel-026",
   "why": "Deletes one price level from two vectors that must move in lockstep. The result is the size at the first matching price, and zero when nothing matches -- a value a genuine zero-size level also produces, so the contract cannot read the result alone. Both vectors are shortened at the same index, which needs a removal characterization of each rather than a length fact. The abort is unstated and comes from the extraction: upstream reaches both vectors through the bulk order, where equal length is structural, so nothing in this body says `sizes` is as long as `prices` and the read at `sizes[i]` aborts when it is not."
  },
